# Module automation — Happy Path + Edge (senior QA)

Before writing or expanding **any** module (Profile drawer, Account, KYC, Fleet, …), do this order every time. Do not skip.

## 1. List cases first (in chat + class Javadoc)

**A. Standard / Happy Path** — expected user journey when everything works:
- Entry (how we open the screen)
- Primary chrome visible (title, key labels, CTAs)
- Successful navigation / actions that must work
- Safe exits (Back, Cancel, Close) that leave Vendor package + correct screen
- Never include destructive confirms in happy path unless the module owns a disposable fixture

**B. Critical Edge Cases** — stress / recover / must-not-break:
- Rapid repeat taps, double open/close
- Dialog Back / Cancel (must not confirm logout, Accept, Decline, Save, Withdraw, …)
- Layout / padding publish checks when dump has bounds
- Recover after dismiss + reopen
- Package stays Vendor; never launcher / wrong app
- Idempotent Cancel / Back chains
- Known-bug documentation only when a case proves it (do not invent)

Write both lists **before** coding. Keep them updated when dump reveals new chrome.

## 2. Automation scripts (TestNG)

Map lists → separate `@Test` methods (one case ≈ one method):

| List | Test class (project convention) | ID prefix |
|------|----------------------------------|-----------|
| Happy Path (identity / chrome) | `*LandingTest` | `XX-L*` |
| Happy Path (user actions) | `*InteractTest` | `XX-I*` |
| Critical Edge | `*EdgeTest` | `XX-E*` |

Rules:
- Each `@Test` has `description` matching the case id + short title
- Prefer dump-sourced locators / Page Object; no blind XPaths
- Standing never-taps: Accept / Decline / Log Out confirm / Withdraw confirm / Save Changes (unless disposable fixture explicitly allowed)
- Chrome-only vs deep module: respect current scope (e.g. Profile drawer chrome before Account page)

## 3. Assertions (hard + soft)

**Hard** (fail fast — journey broken):
- Entry succeeded (`classify…` / `isDisplayedNow`)
- Critical CTA / title present
- Vendor package still `l2b`
- Must-not navigate to launcher / wrong screen after Cancel/Back

Use AssertJ `assertThat(...).as("…").isTrue()` / `isEqualTo(...)` (project default). Equivalent intent to TestNG `Assert.assertTrue` / `Assert.assertEquals`.

**Soft** (collect layout / secondary copy, then report):
- Use `org.assertj.core.api.SoftAssertions` (or `softly.assertThat`) for non-blocking layout bands, optional labels, multi-check publish rows
- Call `softly.assertAll()` at end of that test
- Do **not** soft-assert blocker identity (title / entry / package) — those stay hard

Validate:
- Successful navigation (hard)
- Error / dialog copy when the case opens a dialog (hard for presence; soft OK for secondary wording if flaky)
- Layout spacing / insets (prefer soft batch in one `*-E*` or `*-L*` layout test)

## 4. Per-module checklist (do not forget)

1. Live dump first on agreed account  
2. List Happy Path + Edge in reply  
3. Page Object  
4. Landing + Interact + Edge classes  
5. Isolated suite XMLs + combined `*-all.xml`  
6. Run until green; log real bugs only  
7. Coverage / landing sync when module chrome is done  

This is how we **perform testing in automation** — list → script → assert → run — for **every** module.
